hadiths[174]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4706","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The first instance of Qasamah during the Jahiliyyah involved a man from Banu Hashim who was employed by a man from Quraish"
"4707","Abu Salamah and Sulaiman bin Yasar narrated from one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"4708","it was narrated from Abu Salamah and Sulaiman bin Yasar"
"4709","It was narrated that Ibn Al-Musayyab said:""Qasamah existed during the Jahiliyyah"
"4710","It was narrated from Sahl bin Abi Hathmah that:'Abdullah bin Sahl and Muhayysah set out for Khaibar because of some problem that had arisen. Someone came to Muhayysah and he told him that 'Abdullah bin Sahl had been Killed and thrown into a pit"
"4711","It was narrated from Abu Laila bin 'Abdullah bin 'Abdur-Rahman bin Sahl"
"4712","It was narrated from Yahya"
"4713","(It was narrated from Sahl bin Ab Hathmah and Rafi bin Khadij that:Muhayysah bin Mas'ud and 'Abdullah bin Sahl went to Khaibar for some need they had there"
"4714","It was narrated from Sahi bin Abi Hathmah that:'Abdullah bin SAahi and Nubayysah bin Mas'ud bin Zaid went o Khaibar"
"4715","It was narratd that Sahl bin Abi Hatmah said:""Abdullah bin Sahl and Muhayysah bin Mas'ud bin Zaid went to Khaibar"
"4716","It was narrated from Sahl bin Abi Hathmah that:'Abdullah bin Sahi Al-Anasri and Muhayysah bin Mas'ud went out to Khaibar and went their separate ways to go about their business. 'Abdullah bin Sahl Al-Anasari was killed and Muhayysah. 'Abdur-Rahman"
"4717","It was narrated that Sahl bin Abi Hathmah said:""Abdullah bin Sahl was found slain"
"4718","It was narrated from Bushair bin Yasar that:'Abdullah bin Sahl Al-Ansari and Muhayysah bin Mas'ud went out to Khaibar"
"4719","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin 'Ubaid At-Ta'l from Bushair bin Yasar who said:""A man from among the Ansar who was called Sahl bin Abi Hathmah told him that some of his people went to Khaibar"
"4720","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4721","It was narrated from 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah said:""It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in one of three cases: A soul for a soul"
"4722","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""A man was killed during the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"4723","It was narrated from 'Alqamah binWa'il Al-Hadrami that his farther said:A man who had killed someone was brought to the Messenger of Allah"
"4724","It was narrated that Wa'il said:""I saw the Messenger of Allah when the heir of a victim brought the killer"
"4725","A similar report was narrated from 'Alqamah bin Wa'il from his father"
"4726","It was narrated from 'Alqamah bin Wa'il that his father said:""I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah when a man came with a string around his neck and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4727","Alqamah bin Wa'il narrated from his father that he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah when a man came leading another man by a string. He said:""O Messenger of Allah"
"4728","It was narrated from Simak bin Harb that 'Alqamah bin Wa'il told him that his father said:""I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah when a man came leading another"" (and he narrated) a similar report"
"4729","It was narrated from 'Alqamah bin Wa'il that:his father told them that a man who had killed another man was brought to the Prophet and he handed him over to their of the victim to kill him. Then the Prophet said to those who were sitting with him: ""The killer and the slain will both be in Fire. ""A man went after him and told him that"
"4730","It was narrated from Ans bin Malik that a man brought the killer of his kinsman to the Messenger of Allah and the Prophet said:""Forgive him."" But he refused. He said: ""Take the Diyah"
"4731","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Buraidah"
"4732","It was narrated from Simak"
"4733","It was narrated from Dawud hin Al-Husain"
"4734","It was narrated that Qais bin 'Ubad said:""Al-Ashtar and I went to 'Ali"
"4735","It was narrated from 'Ali"
"4736","It was narrated from Samurah that the Messenger of Allah said:""Whoever kills his slave"
"4737","It was narrated from Samurah that the Prophet said:""Whoever kills his slave"
"4738","It was narrated that Samurah said:""The Prophet said: 'Whoever kills his slave"
"4739","Amr bin Dinar narrated that:he heard Tawus narrate from Ibn 'Abbas"
"4740","It was narrated from Anas that:a Jew killed a young girl for her jewelry"
"4741","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:a Jew took some jewelry from a girl"
"4742","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""A girl went out wearing some jewelry and a Jew caught her"
"4743","It was narrated from 'Aishah"
"4744","It was narrated that Ash-Sha'bi said:""I heard Abu Juhaifah say: 'We asked 'Ali: ""Do you have anything from the Messenger of Allah apart from the Qur'an?"" He said: ""No"
"4745","It was narrated that Abi Hassan said:""Ali said: 'The Messenger of Allah did not tell me anything that he did not tell the people"
"4746","It was narrataed from Al-Ashtar that he said to 'Ali:""What the people have been hearing from you has become widespread. If the Messenger of Allah told you anything"
"4747","Abu Bakrah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever kills a Mu'ahad with no justification"
"4748","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever kills a Mu'ahad with no justification"
"4749","It was narrated from Al-Qasim bin Al-Mukhaimirah"
"4750","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever kills a person from among Ahl Adh-Dhimmah"
"4751","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Hussain that:a slave belonging to some poor people cut off the ear of a slave belonging to some rich people. They came to the Prophet but he did not give them anything"
"4752","It was narrated from Anas that:the Messenger of Allah ruled that Qisas should be given for a tooth. The Messenger of Allah said: ""The Messenger of Allah said: ""What Allah has decreed is retaliation"
"4753","It was narrated from Samurah that the Messenger of Allah said:""Whoever kills his slave"
"4754","It was narrated from Samurah that the Prophet of Allah said:""Whoever castrates his slave"
"4755","It was narrated from Anas that:the sister of Ar-Rubai' Umm Harithah injured a person and they referred the dispute to the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah said: ""Retaliation"
"4756","Anas narrated that:his paternal aunt broke the front tooth of a girl and the Prophet of Allah decreed retaliation. Her brother"
"4757","It was narrated that Anas said:""Ar-Rubai broke the front tooth of a girls"
"4758","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Hussain that:a man bit the hand of another man"
"4759","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Husain that a man bit another man on the forearm:he pulled it away and a front tooth fell out. The matter was referred to the Messenger of Allah and he canceled (the Diyah) and said: ""Did you want to bite your brother's flesh as a stallion bites?"
"4760","It was narrated that 'Imran bin Husain said:""Ya'la fought with a man"
"4761","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Husain that:Ya'la said"
"4762","It was narrated from 'Imran bin Husain that:a man bit another man in the forearm"
"4763","It was narrated from Ya'la bin Munyah that:he fought a man and one of them bit the other"
"4764","It was narrated from Ya'la bin Munyah that:a man from Banu Tamim fought with another man"
"4765","It was narrated from Safwan bin 'Abdullah that his two paternal uncles"
"4766","It was narrated from Safwan bin Ya'la"
"4767","It was narrated from Ya'la that:he hired a worker who fought with a man and bit his hand"
"4768","It was narrated from Safwan bin Ya'la that his father said:""I went on the campaign to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah"
"4769","It was narrated that Ya'la bin Umayyah said:""I went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah in the Army of Hardship"
"4770","A similar report to that of the one who bit (another man) and his from tooth fell out was narrated from Ibn Ya'la from his father"
"4771","It was narrated from Safwan bin Ya'la bin Munyah that:a hired man of Ya'la bin Munyah was bitten by another on his forearm and he pulled it away from his mouth. The matter was referred to the Prophet"
"4772","It was narrated from Safwan bin Ya'la that:his father wen on the campaign of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah"
"4773","It was narrated that Abu Aa'eed Al-Khudri daid:""While the Messenger of Allah was distributing something"
"4774","It was narrated the Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:""While the Messenger of Allah was distributing something"
"4775","Ibn 'Abbad narrated that:a man slandered one of his forefathers from the time of the Jahiliyyah"
"4776","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""We would sit with the Messenger of Allah in the Masjid and when he stood up"
"4777","It was narrated from Abu Firas that ""Umar said:""I saw the Messenger of Allah allowing others to seek retaliation against him"
"4778","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:the Messenger of Allah sent Abu Jahm bin Hudhaifah to collect Zakah and a man argued with him about his Sadaqah"
"4779","It was narrated from Anas"
"4780","It was narrated from Anas that:the Messenger of Allah sent a detachment jof troops to some people of Khath'am"
"4781","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""There was Qisas among the Children of Israel"
"4782","It was narrated that Mujahid said:""Al-Qisas (the Law of Equality in punishment) is prescribed for you in case of murder: the free for the free[2] The rule for the Children of Israel was Qisas"
"4783","It was narrated that Anas said:""A case requiring Qisas was brought to the Messenger of Allah and he enjoined them to pardon"
"4784","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""No case requiring Qisas was ever brought to the Messenger of Allah but he would enjoin pardoning"
"4785","Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'If a person's relative is killed"
"4786","Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'If a person's relative is killed"
"4787","Abu Salamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:""If a person's relative is killed."" In Mursal form. (Shah)"
"4788","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:""And it is upon those (relatives) of the killed one to block (any punishment) the first (in line) then the first"
"4789","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever is killed in the blind or by something thrown"
"4790","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbad"
"4791","It was narrated from Al-Qasim bin Rabi'ah"
"4792","It was narrated from Al-Qasim bin Rabi'ah that:the Messenger of Allah delivered a speech on the Day of the Conquest. (And he mentioned it) in Mursal from"
"4793","It was narrated from Abdullah bin 'Amr that the prophet said:""Indeed the accidental killing"
"4794","It was narrated from 'Uqbah bin Aws"
"4795","It was narrated from 'Uqbah bin 'Aws"
"4796","It was narrated from Ya'qub bin Aws"
"4797","It was narrated from Ya'qub bin Aws that:a man from among the Companions of the Prophet told him"
"4798","It was narrated from Ya'qub bin Aws that:a man from among the Companions of the Prophet narrated to him that the Prophet entered Makkah during the Year of the Conquest"
"4799","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah stood up on the Day of the Conquest of Makkah"
"4800","It was narrated from Al- Qasim bin Rabi'ah that the Messenger jof Allah said:""The accident that resembles on purpose"
"4801","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4802","In Mas'ud said:""The Messenger of Allah ruled that the Diyah for accidental killing is twenty Bint Makhad"
"4803","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""A man killed another man during the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"4804","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:the Prophet ruled that twelve thousand (should be given) as Diyah. (Hahan)"
"4805","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4806","It was narrated from 'Amr Bin Shu'aib"
"4807","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4808","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah ruled that the Diyah for a Mukatab who is killed should be (equivalent) to the Diyah for a free mand"
"4809","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:the Prophet of Allah ruled that the Diyah for a Mukatab should be (equivalent) to the Diyah for a free man"
"4810","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah ruled that in the case of a Mukatab"
"4811","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas tht the Prophet said:""The Mukatab is free to the extent that the has paid off (toward buying his freedom); he Hadd punishment should be carried out on him proportionate to the amount he has paid off (toward buying his freedom); and he inherits proportionate to the amount he has paid off (toward buying his freedom)"
"4812","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:a Mukatab was killed at the time of the Messenger of Allah and he commanded that the Diyah be paid (equivalent) to the Diyah for a free man"
"4813","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Buraidah"
"4814","Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated that:a woman threw pebbles at another woman and the woman who was struck miscarried. The matter was referred to the prophet and he set the blood money for her child at five hundred sheep. And on that day"
"4815","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Mughaffal that he saw a man throwing pebbles and he said:""Do not throw pebbles"
"4816","Hamal bin Malik said:""The Messenger of Allah ruled that a slave (should be given as Diyah) for a fetus."" Tawus said: ""A horse would do in place of a slave"
"4817","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah ruled that a male or female slave should be given (as Diyah) to a woman of Banu Lihyah whosw child was miscarried and died. Then the woman to whom he had decreed that the slave should be given died"
"4818","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""Two women of Hudhail had a fight"
"4819","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:there were two women of Hudhail during the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"4820","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab that:the Messenger of Allah ruled that for a fetus which is killed in the mother's womb"
"4821","It was narrated from Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah that:a woman struck her co-wife with a tent pole and killed her"
"4822","It was narrated that Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah said:""A woman struck her co-wife"
"4823","It was narrated from Al-Mughirah bin shu'bah that:there were two co-wives"
"4824","It was narrated that Al-Muhgirah bin Shu'bah said:""A woman of Banu Lihyan struck her co-wife with a tent pole and killed her"
"4825","It was narrated from Al-Muhgirah b in Shu'bad that:two woman were married to a man of Hudhail"
"4826","It was narrated form Al-Mughirahbin shu'bah that:a man of Hudhail had two wives"
"4827","It was narrated from al-a'mash from Ibrahim who said:""I woman struck her co-wife"
"4828","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said; ""There were two women neighbors between whom there was some trouble. One of them threw a rock at the other a she miscarried a boy - whose hair had already grown -0 who was or dead"
"4829","Jabir said:""The Messenger of Allah ruled that every clan should take part in paying the blood money"
"4830","It was narrated from'Amrbin shu'aib"
"4831","Narrator mentioned in hadith:A similar report was narrated from 'Amr bin shu'aib"
"4832","It was narrated that Abu Rimthah said; ""I came to the Prophet with my father and he said:'Who is this with you?' He said:' my son"
"4833","It was narrated that Tha'labah bin Zahdam said:""some people from Banu Tha'labah came to the Prophet when he was delivering a speech and a man said; ""O Messenger of Allah"
"4834","It was narrated that Tha'1abah bin Zahdam said:""Some people from Banu Tha'labah came to the Prophet (ﷺ) when he was delivering a speech and a man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4835","It was narrated that Ash'ath bin Abi Ash-Sha'tha"
"4836","It was narrated from Al-Aswad bin Hilal - who met the Prophet - from a man from Banu Tha'labah bin Yarbu"
"4837","It was narrated from Al-Ash'ath bin sulaim"
"4838","It was narrated from Ash'ath"
"4839","It was narrated from Tariq and Muharibi that a manh said:""O Messenger of Allah"
"4840","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4841","It was narrated from'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4842","It was narrated from 'Amr bin shu'aib"
"4843","It was narrated fromabu MUsa that the Prophet said:""For fingers (the Diyah is ) ten (camels) each"
"4844","It was narrated from Abu Musa Al-Asha'ari that the Prophet of Allah said:""Fingers are the same"
"4845","It was narrated that Abu Musa said:""The Messenger of Allah ruled that the fingers are the same and (the Diyah is ) ten camels for each"
"4846","It was narrated from Sa'eed bin al-Musayyab that:when the letter was found that was with the family of 'Amr bin Hazm"
"4847","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that the Propher said:""this and this are the same"
"4848","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas:""This and this are the same: The little finger and the thumb (sahih)"
"4849","It was narrated that Ibn 'abbas said:""The (Diyah for) fingers are ten each"
"4850","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""When the Messenger of Allah conquered Makkah"
"4851","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"4852","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib that his father told him that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) conquered Makkah "
"4853","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin 'Amr bin Hazm"
"4854","It was narrated from Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin 'Amr bin Hazm"
"4855","It was narrated that Ibn shihab said:""I read the letter of the Messenger of allah which he wrote for 'Amr bin Hazm when he sent him to govern Najran. The letter was with Abu Bakr bin Hazm. The Messenger of Allah wrote this; 'A statement from Allah and His Messenger; O you who believe! Fulfill (your) obligations"
"4856","It was narrate that Az-Zuhri said:""Abu Bakr bin Hazm brought me a letter on a piece of leather (which was ) from the Messenger of Allah: 'This is a statement from Allah and His Messenger: 'O you who believe! Fulfill (your obligations. And he quoted some Verses from it. Then he said: 'For a soul"
"4857","It was narrated from' Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin 'Amr bin Hazm that his rather said:""The letter which the Messenger of Allah wrote to 'Amr bin Hazm concerning blood money: 'For a soul"
"4858","It was narrated form Anas bin Malik that:a Bedouin came to the door of the prophet and put his eye to the crack. The Prophet saw him and intended to put his eye out with a sword or a stick. When he saw him "
"4859","It was narrated from Sahl bin Sa'd As-Saidi that:a man looked through a hole in the door of the Prophet"
"4860","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:""Whoever looks into a house without the permission of the occupants and they put out his eye"
"4861","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:""If a person were to look at you without permission and you were to throw a stone at him and put out his eye"
"4862","It was narrated from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri that:he was praying and a son a Marwan wanted to pass in front of him. He tried to stop him but he did not go back"
"4863","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:""Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Laila told me to ask Ibn 'Abbas about two Verses: 'And whoever kills a believe"
"4864","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jabair said:""The people of Al-Kufah differed concerning this verse: 'And whoever kills a believer intentionally. So I went to Ibn 'Abbas and asked him"
"4865","It was narrated that Sa'eed bin Jubair said:""I said to Ibn Abbas . 'Can a person who killed a believer intentionally repent?' He said: 'No.' Irecited the Verse from Al-Furqan to him: And those who invoke not any other ilah (god) along with Allah"
"4866","It was narrated from Salim bin abi Ja'd that:Ibn 'Abbas was asked about someone who killed a believer deliberately then he repented"
"4867","It was narrated that 'Ubaidullah bin abi Bakr said:""I heard Ana's say: 'The Messenger of Allah said: 'the major sins are; associating others with Allah (shirk)"
"4868","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr that the Prophet said:""The major sins are: associating others with Allah"
"4869","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'No one who commits Zina is a believer at the moment when he is committing Zina"
"4870","It was narrated from abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah said:""No one who commits Zina is a believer at the moment when he is committing Zina; no one who steals is a believe at the moment when he is stealing; no one who drinks wine is a believer at the moment when he is drinking it; and no robber is a believer at the moment when he is robbing and the people are looking on"
"4871","It was narrated from abu Hurairah that the Prophet - and Ahmad said in his Hadith:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'No one who commits Zina is a believer at the moment when he is committing Zina; no one who steals is a believer at the moment when he is stealing; no one who drinks wine is a believer at the moment when he is drinking it; but repentance is available to him after that"
"4872","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""No one who commits Zina is a believer at the moment when he is committing Zina; no one who steals is a believer at the moment when he is stealing; no one who drinks wine is a believer at the moment when he is drinking it."" - And he mentioned a fourth but I (the narrator) have forgotten it - ""When he does that the yoke of Islam is shed from his neck"
"4873","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah"
"4874","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Bashir that:a group of the Kala'iyin complaned to him about some people who had stolen some goods"
"4875","It was narrated from Bahz bin Hakim"
"4876","It was narrated from Bahz bin Hakim"
"4877","It was narrated from abu Umayah Al-Makhzumi that:a thief who confused to a crime but with whom no stolen goods has been found"
"4878","It was narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah"
"4879","It was narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah that:a man stole his Burdah"